course: dictionary
lesson: 6043
title: Memorandum: a short formal note
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A memorandum is a formal word for a short written message. Offices, schools and companies send them to tell people about something important. Everyday people shorten it to «memo», so a memo and a memorandum are the same thing.
explain: The word also has two other meanings. A memorandum can be a note that helps you remember something. In law, a memorandum of understanding is a written agreement between two groups or countries. «In 1991 Ukraine had the world's third-largest stock of nuclear weapons on its soil» tells you the setting is serious, and «under the 1994 Budapest Memorandum it gave them up for assurances» shows that a memorandum here is a written promise between countries.
explain: Use the clues around the word to choose the meaning. If the words mention an office, a school or a company, it is probably the short message. If they mention countries, promises or agreements, it is the law meaning.
fact: A memorandum is a formal word for a short written message.
fact: «Memo» is the everyday short form of memorandum.
fact: The plural of memorandum can be memoranda or memorandums.
fact: A memorandum of understanding is a written agreement between two groups or countries.
fact: In «the Budapest Memorandum», Ukraine gave up its nuclear weapons in 1994 in return for promises from the USA, the UK and Russia to respect its borders.
exercise: «In 1991 Ukraine had the world's third-largest stock of nuclear weapons on its soil.» Under the 1994 Budapest Memorandum, what did Ukraine do? | Sent a memo to every school | *Gave up its nuclear weapons for promises to respect its borders | Moved its borders into Russia | Built even more nuclear weapons
exercise: The head teacher sent a memorandum to every class about the sports day. What is a memorandum in this sentence? | *A short written message | A type of sports equipment | A nuclear weapon | A song sung at assembly
exercise: Which phrase names a written agreement between two countries? | A memorandum of lunch | A memorandum of rain | A memo to remember your homework | *A memorandum of understanding
test: Pick the meaning of memorandum when it is a note to help you remember something. | A loud announcement at a football match | A written agreement between countries | A type of office chair | *A note that helps you remember something
test: What is the everyday short form of memorandum? | Memoir | *Memo | Memory | Mem
exam: In the sentence «the wise thing is to ask parents and grandparents about the history they lived», what is the best way to find out the meaning of a hard word? | Ask the nearest pet to help | Guess a random meaning without thinking | *Read the words around it and use the context clues | Give up and skip the sentence completely
